# Derived by hand from Appendix B (`!Both` fires in a tick in which both events fire, with the pair) and Type System ch. 4 (the call in the plain function is not lifted; `Total` is lifted over its firing): the first click fires the left alone and nothing is heard; the second tick fires both, 1 + 2. Never run.
test t

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="left")
    1: Ui.Button(label="right")
    2: Ui.Label(text="0: 0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click

tick 2
  in:
    0: click
    1: click
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="1: 3")
